<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33732" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pappus</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάππος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An old man</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 30</span></i>
			Müll.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>A grandfather</i>, <i><span class="en">Aus.
				Idyll. 4, 18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The woolly</i>, <i>hairy seed of
				certain plants</i>, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 3, 386</span></i> Lachm.; also ap. <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				220</span></i> Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">semen ei lanuginis, quam pappon vocant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					21, 16, 57, § 97</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A plant</i>, <i>also called</i>
			erigeron: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quare eam Callimachus acanthida appellat, alii
					pappum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					25, 13, 106, § 168</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
